|~ `::construct`, the step that puts a value under a tag through the
   tag's constructor, `::T<payload>`, and the refusals of that step. ~|

::construct
  |~~ The step of a constructor invocation, `::T<payload>`: it puts a
      payload under the tag `::T` through the tag's constructor, which
      checks or builds the value. As a record, `:tag` is the tag and
      `:payload` the step of its payload. ::link~(::tag | doc)
      ::link~(::qlang | doc :pipeline)

      ~(~(::Box[1 2]) | first | [/tag /payload] | eq [::Box [1 2]])
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/type/construct}

::ConstructPayloadNotSchemaError
  |~~ A ::construct payload is a Map of `:tag` a tag and `:payload` a
      step.
      ::link~(::construct | doc)

      ~(
        ::construct{:tag :Box :payload [1]}
        !| [type /field]
        |  eq [::ConstructPayloadNotSchemaError :tag]
       )
  ~~|

::ConstructReadBackDiffersError
  |~~ The ::construct prints as text that reads back as another step: a
      payload that opens with a name, a digit or a slash is written
      as a group.
      ::link~(::construct | doc)

      ~(
        ::construct{:tag ::Box :payload 42}
        !| [type /printed]
        |  eq [::ConstructReadBackDiffersError "::Box42"]
       )
  ~~|

::TagBindingHasNoConstructorError
  |~~ Tag-binding has no registered constructor — `:impl`
      carries an unexpected value (neither a `:qlang/prim/*`
      keyword nor a Quote-impl body). Descriptor fields:
      `:payloadValue` / `:payloadType`, `:actualValue` /
      `:actualType`, `:expectedType [:keyword :quote]`.
      ::link~(::construct | doc)
  ~~|

::TaggedLitNotTagBindingError
  |~~ `::tag` constructor invocation — the env binding under
      `::tag` is not a tag-binding descriptor Map.
      ::link~(::construct | doc)

      ~(
        ::badType 42 | ::badType[]
        !| [type /tag /actualType]
        |  eq [::TaggedLitNotTagBindingError :badType ::number]
       )
  ~~|
